//? Title: Score SDE: Reverse Diffusion and Probability Flow
//? Subtitle: Native tensor components with editable training and sampling loops
//? Requires: noise_conditional_score.mepml
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
This report preserves the original score_sde experiment and moves reusable tensor operations into datamunge. Parameter stores, objectives, minibatch loops, optimizer writes and sampling trajectories are visible in the complete program.
)
\toc

> Method, preserved protocol and observed limitations

[Song et al., Score-Based Generative Modeling through Stochastic Differential Equations (2020)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2011.13456) relates reverse diffusion and probability-flow dynamics. This report freezes the preceding NCSN and conditions its predictor continuously at level15*(1-t). It uses sigma(t)=.05*20^t, retaining the source Float32 logarithm constants, and g²=2*log(20)*sigma².

For descending physical time, the source reverse drift is g²*score and its probability-flow drift is half that. The editable caller evaluates64 Euler-Maruyama steps with explicit innovations and 8/16/32 classical RK4 probability-flow steps. All RK4 stages, state-only gradients, discrete conditioning checks and Gaussian-oracle refinement runs are retained. The ODE ignores innovation exactly; changing SDE innovations changes samples. Agreement of continuous conditioning with the 16 training levels has maximum score residual7.152557373e-7. The terminal conditional-prior KL bound is 27.931187297 per image, highlighting a substantial terminal-prior mismatch. This experiment does not establish likelihood accuracy or sample quality.

> Follow the state through one model operation

The method diagram separates the explicitly supplied state and conditioning from the predictor and the single transition. The caller owns repeated transitions and training.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/score_sde_method.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){std::filesystem::create_directories("build");dm::graphics::Diagram d(28,1150);dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle s;s.width=11;s.height=5;s.font_size=30;d.node("input",{-18,0},"State + physical t\nDescending time",s).node("predict",{-5,0},"Frozen NCSN score\nVE coefficients",s).node("step",{8,0},"EM or RK4 step\nExplicit EM noise",s).node("loop",{21,0},"Caller trajectory\nRetain all stages",s).edge("input","predict").edge("predict","step").edge("step","loop").save_svg("build/score_sde_method.svg");}
```
